{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvuTyGRSesNGTibX6SzS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QjLkrr62CxHMs7UuZaQcML","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n -i \"control\" paper.tex | grep -n -i \"match\\|abstract\\|conclu\\|non-vacu\\|invarian\" | cut -c1-400; sed -n 30,42p paper.tex | cut -c1-1500; cat .claude/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json | head -150"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2122,"cache_read_input_tokens":50959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2122},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff70e5e4-c0ea-42eb-940e-6ce62303ebf1","uuid":"325a39a9-3dc1-495f-a875-1516544d9708","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:29:25.609Z","request_id":"req_011CgvuTxkfHG5B5m4QKkC2e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QjLkrr62CxHMs7UuZaQcML","type":"tool_result","content":"6:134:\\emph{Main efficiency} averages over boards, over main cases (8 rules $\\times$ 2 targets $\\times$ 2 cost measures per board) and over evaluator seeds. \\emph{Control efficiency} averages two conditions per board and rule: a permuted-input control (non-identity row and task permutations, reference cost invariant) and a within-task shuffled-score null (columns shuffled across models, target set\n11:163:The retained control efficiency of 1.0002 indicates that, on permuted instances and on shuffled-null matrices, verified plan costs matched their own references on average to within about $2\\times10^{-4}$. These controls check invariance to row and task order and non-vacuity of the instance; they do not probe whether the planner overfits the Open LLM boards. The evaluator recomputes every pl\n\\title{Verified Minimal-Investment Planning for Leaderboard Rank Targeting under Multiple Aggregation Rules}\n\\iclrfinalcopy\n\\author{Anonymous authors}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nMulti-task leaderboards turn a matrix of per-task scores into a single ranking through an aggregation rule, and a developer who can raise a target model's score on selected tasks, for example by training on related data, may be able to push it to first place. How much such targeted investment is needed, and how that quantity depends on the aggregation rule, is the question that motivates this work. We formalize targeted investment as non-negative, independent per-task score gains, priced either by total points (L1) or by the number of tasks touched (L0), with success meaning the target is strictly first under eight rules (mean, median, trimmed mean, z-score mean, Borda, plurality, Copeland, maximin). We then study a verification-first planner that returns the cheapest plan it can certify, combining exact solvers for four rules with verified heuristics for the others. On two held-out Open LLM Leaderboard boards, scored by a trusted evaluator against its own reference solver, the planner reaches a mean efficiency of 1.0032 relative to the reference, against 0.8166 for the better of two naive baselines, with every response well-formed; the evaluation is qualified. Because per-rule costs were not retained, we do \\emph{not} test whether required investment varies across rules, and the results say nothing about real training effects.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Introduction}\nMulti-task benchmarks are the standard instrument for comparing machine-learning models: a leaderboard collects scores of many models on many sub-datasets and an aggregation rule, most often the arithmetic mean, converts each model's score vector into a rank \\citep{Hendrycks2020MeasuringMM,Liang2022HolisticEO}. Rankings influence adoption, publication and funding, so developers have an incentive to act on them, which is the familiar pattern in which a metric used as a target ceases to measure what it was meant to measure \\citep{Thomas2020RelianceOM}. One class of actions is to include data related to some of the sub-datasets in a model's training, which raises its scores on those tasks. Prior work documents that leaderboards are sensitive to task selection \\citep{Dehghani2021TheBL}, to aggregation choices \\citep{Colombo2022WhatAT,Rofin2022VotenRankRO,Lanctot2023EvaluatingAU}, to private testing and uneven sampling \\citep{Singh2025TheLI}, and to benchmark leakage \\citep{Zhou2023DontMY,Sainz2023NLPEI,Yang2023RethinkingBA}. What remains less examined is a quantitative, rule-by-rule account of how large a targeted investment must be for a specific model to reach first place.\n{\n  \"$defs\": {\n    \"FigureFontSizes\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"description\": \"Explicit font sizes for the legacy manifest contract.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"axis\": {\n          \"title\": \"Axis\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"legend\": {\n          \"title\": \"Legend\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"ticks\": {\n          \"title\": \"Ticks\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"title\": {\n          \"title\": \"Title\",\n          \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"title\",\n        \"axis\",\n        \"ticks\",\n        \"legend\"\n      ],\n      \"title\": \"FigureFontSizes\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"LegacyFigureManifestFigure\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": false,\n      \"allOf\": [\n        {\n          \"else\": {\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"path_pdf\": {\n                \"minLength\": 1\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\n              \"path_pdf\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"if\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"generator\": {\n                    \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"generator\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"attempted_generator\": {\n                    \"const\": \"generate-concept-figure\"\n                  },\n                  \"fallback_reason\": {\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"generator\": {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  },\n                  \"prompt_log_path\": {\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"generator\",\n                  \"attempted_generator\",\n                  \"prompt_log_path\",\n                  \"fallback_reason\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original flat figure-manifest entry shape.\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"attempted_generator\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"generate-concept-figure\",\n                \"matplotlib\",\n                \"tikz\",\n                \"native_latex\",\n                \"manual\"\n              ],\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Attempted Generator\"\n        },\n        \"categories_per_panel\": {\n          \"items\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          \"title\": \"Categories Per Panel\",\n          \"type\": \"array\"\n        },\n        \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"exclusiveMinimum\": 0,\n              \"type\": \"number\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Estimated Min Rendered Font Pt\"\n        },\n        \"fallback_reason\": {\n          \"anyOf\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"null\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"default\": null,\n          \"title\": \"Fallback Reason\"\n        },\n        \"figure_id\": {\n          \"minLength\": 1,\n          \"title\": \"Figure Id\",\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"figure_type\": {\n          \"enum\": [\n            \"grouped_bar\",\n            \"bar\",\n            \"line\",\n            \"box\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff70e5e4-c0ea-42eb-940e-6ce62303ebf1","uuid":"4acac4d4-fa3a-4912-b814-d9f6fe4400bc","timestamp":"2026-11-11T09:29:25.667Z","tool_u